      "justification": "End-tidal CO2 monitoring provides real-time feedback on CPR quality and can serve as a prognostic indicator. A value >10 mmHg suggests adequate CPR, and a sudden rise may indicate ROSC. This is recommended by ACLS guidelines during cardiac arrest management."
    },
